<title>USA: USDA fine-tunes 97/98 crop projections.</title>
<headline>USDA fine-tunes 97/98 crop projections.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Department of Agriculture analysts present updated estimates for 1997/98 U.S. crop production at the annual Outlook Forum on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The new figures were based on conditions in early February and, in some cases, superceded the long-term baseline estimates that were released in printed material on Monday, the opening day of the USDA conference.</p>
<p>The baseline projections were compiled during November and December as part of preparation of the fiscal 1998 budget.</p>
<p>USDA speakers on Monday at the Outlook Forum revealed parts of the updated estimates that were issued Tuesday, although the speakers sometimes rounded off the figures.</p>
</text>
